<h1>MCP tool definitions and how they change</h1>
<p class="lead">HISTOR reads the tool list of every remote MCP server in the official MCP registry once a day, and runs every
new version of npm and PyPI MCP packages in a sandbox. Once a week the whole record is published here as files:
what each server advertised, and every change, field by field. Free under CC BY 4.0.</p>
<div class="stats">
<div class="stat"><b>96,101</b><span>listed servers and packages</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>112,557</b><span>distinct tool lists</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>73,198</b><span>recorded changes</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>16,758</b><span>servers changed at least once</span></div>
</div>
<h2>Latest snapshot: 2026-11-09</h2>
<div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Rows</th><th>Size</th><th>What</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/servers.jsonl.gz"><code>servers.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">103,271</td><td class="n">22.8 MB</td><td>One row per listed server: endpoint, transport, status, tool count, the digest of its current tool list.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/toolsets.jsonl.gz"><code>toolsets.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">112,557</td><td class="n">1,586.1 MB</td><td>Every tool list a server served (name, description and schemas, as served), current ones and every one a change replaced.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/changes.jsonl.gz"><code>changes.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">73,198</td><td class="n">76.4 MB</td><td>Every recorded change: tools added, removed and modified, field by field, with the signed label.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/scans.jsonl.gz"><code>scans.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">26,235</td><td class="n">1.8 MB</td><td>WARDEN pattern matches per tool list (rules in pattern-set.json). Leads to read, not verdicts.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/classifications.jsonl.gz"><code>classifications.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">4,194</td><td class="n">233 kB</td><td>Advisory LLM readings of tool lists. Not reproducible, so never in the signed log.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/tool_extras.jsonl.gz"><code>tool_extras.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">147,528</td><td class="n">61.2 MB</td><td>What each tool carried beyond those: annotations (readOnlyHint, destructiveHint…), _meta, title, icons. Since 2026-10-22.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/extras_changes.jsonl.gz"><code>extras_changes.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">180,931</td><td class="n">19.2 MB</td><td>Every change to those members, annotation by annotation, with the tools that dropped readOnlyHint.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/package_observations.jsonl.gz"><code>package_observations.jsonl.gz</code></a></td><td class="n">227,788</td><td class="n">18.8 MB</td><td>Every run of an npm/PyPI package with the version it ran and the list it served. Versions since 2026-10-26.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/manifest.json"><code>manifest.json</code></a></td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td>Counts and SHA-256 of every file, signed by the log&#x27;s key, with the tree head of the snapshot.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="2026-11-09/README.md"><code>README.md</code></a></td><td class="n"></td><td class="n"></td><td>The dataset card: fields, loading, citation, what the data does not say.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p><b>New here?</b> Start with <code>servers.jsonl.gz</code> (one row per listed server) and <code>changes.jsonl.gz</code>
(one row per recorded change, field by field); <code>toolsets.jsonl.gz</code> is the large one — every distinct tool list in full.
Sizes are in the table.</p>
<p>The same files: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions">Hugging Face</a> (one tag per snapshot) ·
<a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759">Zenodo</a> (a DOI per archived snapshot; the record names its date, and <a href="latest/">latest/</a> here may be newer) ·
<a href="latest/">latest/</a> always points at the newest snapshot.</p>
<h2>Load it</h2>
<pre>from datasets import load_dataset   # Hugging Face, typed changes configuration
changes = load_dataset("alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions", name="changes", split="train")</pre>
<pre>-- DuckDB: the servers whose tool lists changed most often
SELECT s.name, count(*) AS changes
FROM 'https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/changes.jsonl.gz' c
JOIN 'https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/servers.jsonl.gz' s ON s.id = c.serverId
GROUP BY s.name ORDER BY changes DESC LIMIT 20;</pre>
<pre>import pandas as pd
servers = pd.read_json("https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/servers.jsonl.gz", lines=True)</pre>
<h2>Cite</h2>
<p class="cite">Artamokhov, A. (2026). <i>HISTOR snapshot 2026-11-02: MCP tool definitions and how they change</i> [Data set].
Zenodo. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23884408">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23884408</a></p>
<p>The latest snapshot, 2026-11-09, is not on Zenodo yet; the citation above is the newest one that is. To cite 2026-11-09 itself, give its signed manifest: <a href="2026-11-09/manifest.json">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/2026-11-09/manifest.json</a>.</p>
<p>Cite the snapshot you counted on: the same query gives other numbers on another snapshot. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512759</a> stands for all of them and always opens the newest.</p>
<h2>Check it</h2>
<p><code>manifest.json</code> lists the SHA-256 of every file and is signed (Ed25519) by the log's key
<code>did:key:z6Mkw1CVxsPj9utYp7VXWEbuuGM9Ev47itwKu1UfKd5ByxR9</code>, with the signed tree head the snapshot was taken under. Any label in it can be
proven against the live log: <a href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/">https://histor.modelmarket.dev</a>. Code: <a href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor">https://github.com/alexar76/histor</a>.</p>
<h2>All snapshots</h2>
<ul><li><a href="2026-11-09/">2026-11-09</a> · 96,101 servers · 73,198 changes</li><li><a href="2026-11-02/">2026-11-02</a> · 90,863 servers · 53,159 changes · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23884408">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23884408</a></li><li><a href="2026-10-26/">2026-10-26</a> · 85,913 servers · 31,660 changes · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23884119">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23884119</a></li><li><a href="2026-10-25/">2026-10-25</a> · 85,437 servers · 30,151 changes · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23881379">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23881379</a></li><li><a href="2026-10-20/">2026-10-20</a> · 81,879 servers · 23,821 changes · <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512760">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512760</a></li></ul>
<h2>What it does not say</h2>
<ul>
<li>A tool list is what a server showed an anonymous client on that day; servers that need a key show less or nothing.</li>
<li>A change is a change in the definitions, not a judgement. Most are ordinary releases.</li>
<li>Pattern matches and classifier flags are text worth reading, not proof that a server is malicious.</li>
<li>A server operator who wants out of future snapshots can open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor">https://github.com/alexar76/histor</a>.</li>
</ul>
</main></body></html>
